build	refused	Parse error at 12:16: `func pair` may not return a reference: the return type `(Int, &Int)` names a reference (`&Int`), and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106; the Law of Exclusivity is statically sound only because every live reference belongs to a call still on the stack). Returning one hands back a pointer into the frame that just died. Return the value instead (drop the `&`: `&Int` becomes `Int`), or — to hand out storage the receiver already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141), which lends the place for a window rather than letting a pointer out
